ater & Burst Pipe Claim Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/burst-pipe-water-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Claim Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/house-fire-smoke-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wildfire, Ember & Smoke Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/wildfire-ember-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Snow Load & Ice Dam Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/snow-load-ice-dam-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance Estimate Review","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/carrier-estimate-second-look/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/neutral-umpire/"}}]},"description":"Independent insurance appraisal, estimate review and umpire services for disputed hail, wind, snow, water and fire claims in all 23 Wyoming counties.","areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"},{"@type":"City","name":"Cheyenne","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Casper","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Laramie","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Gillette","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Rock Springs","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Sheridan","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Green River","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Evanston","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Riverton","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Jackson","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Cody","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Rawlins","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}}],"priceRange":"$$","knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Hail damage","Wind damage","Snow load","Xactimate estimating","Umpire services"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Wyoming Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#webpage","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/","name":"How Insurance Appraisal Works in Wyoming | 8 Steps","description":"A step-by-step guide to insurance appraisal in Wyoming: the written demand, naming appraisers, choosing an umpire, panel work and the award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-11","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/inspector-clipboard.webp","width":1024,"height":778},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#howto"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal step by step","item":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/"}],"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How insurance appraisal works in Wyoming","description":"The steps of a property insurance appraisal from the first disagreement to a signed award.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Pin down the disagreement","text":"Before anything formal happens, write down exactly what you disagree with: which items are missing, which measurements are short, which prices are low, and what your contractor’s number is. Send it to the carrier with photos. A documented supplement request closes a lot of gaps on its own, and it gives you a record if it doesn’t.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Read the appraisal condition","text":"Find the paragraph titled “Appraisal” in the conditions section of your policy. Note who can demand it, how many days each side has to name an appraiser, how the umpire is chosen, and whether anything else — like a sworn proof of loss — must come first. Find the “Suit Against Us” condition too.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Send a written demand","text":"Either side may demand appraisal. The demand should identify the policy and claim, say that you disagree on the amount of loss, invoke the appraisal provision and name your appraiser or commit to naming one within the policy’s window. Send it in a way you can prove, such as certified mail plus email.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Both appraisers are named","text":"Each side picks a competent, independent appraiser. Yours inspects the property, measures everything and builds a line-item estimate. The carrier’s appraiser does the same. They exchange estimates and begin comparing.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"The umpire is selected","text":"The two appraisers agree on a neutral umpire, ideally early so one is ready if needed. If they can’t agree within the policy’s time limit, either side can usually ask a court of record in the county where the property is — in Wyoming, typically the district court — to appoint one.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"The appraisers work it out","text":"This is where most of the money moves. The appraisers walk the property together, compare quantities and prices, and agree on every item they can. Many Wyoming appraisals end here with both appraisers signing an agreed award.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"The umpire decides what’s left","text":"Each appraiser submits a written position on the remaining items with photos, measurements and pricing support. The umpire may visit the property or meet with both appraisers, then decides each item.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"The award is signed and paid","text":"An award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. A good award separates replacement cost, depreciation and actual cash value by coverage. The carrier then pays under the policy terms, less the deductible and prior payments, with recoverable depreciation released when repairs are done.","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#step-8"}],"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-step-by-step/#howto"}]}</script>
</head>
